From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: orangepi-zero2: enable the expansion board USB host ports

USB 2 and 3 of the H616 are routed to the Zero2's 13-pin header, where
the official expansion board provides two USB-A ports. Enable their
EHCI/OHCI controllers so U-Boot can boot from a USB stick plugged in
there as well as in the on-board USB-A port (ehci1/ohci1). Same change
as Armbian's kernel patch
arm64-dts-sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2-enable-expansion-board-usb.patch.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff -ruN a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
--- a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
+++ b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
@@ -69,6 +69,13 @@
 };
 
 /* USB 2 & 3 are on headers only. */
+&ehci2 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ehci3 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
 
 &emac0 {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
@@ -99,6 +106,14 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&ohci2 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ohci3 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &spi0  {
 	status = "okay";
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
